From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: restore MSM8226 contexts on runtime resume

SM-T531 display context0 reads all zeros after the first runtime suspend
and resume, despite a registered software domain. Holding the IOMMU on
before loading DRM preserves SCTLR/TTBR/TCR/MAIR, removes the MDP underrun
and produces real page flips at 59.98-59.99 Hz. The DSI bridge still fails
separately, so this does not establish working LCD output.

Replay the cached non-secure context after the existing SCM restore on
MSM8226. Keep TrustZone in charge of global registers and secure banks.
Do not hold the domain permanently powered; other compatibles retain their
existing resume behavior. Balance clocks on SCM errors.

Uses Dmitry Baryshkov's context caching refactor (preceding patch).
The resume approach is adapted from [PATCH 07/12] of his v1 series:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260809-msm8974-iommu-upstream-v1-7-87f5cd492560@oss.qualcomm.com
That patch's OS-managed MSM8974 global setup is deliberately not imported:
MSM8226 display global IDR0 access was verified to abort non-secure reads.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 65039aada..96cb05654 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ struct qcom_iommu_dev {
 	void __iomem		*local_base;
 	u32			 sec_id;
 	u8			 max_asid;
+	bool			 restore_ctx;
 	struct qcom_iommu_ctx	*ctxs[];   /* indexed by asid */
 };
 
@@ -805,6 +806,8 @@ static int qcom_iommu_device_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	qcom_iommu->max_asid = max_asid;
 	qcom_iommu->dev = dev;
+	qcom_iommu->restore_ctx = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
+							"qcom,msm8226-iommu");
 
 	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
 	if (res) {
@@ -905,14 +908,32 @@ static void qcom_iommu_device_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(CLK_NUM, qcom_iommu->clks);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (dev->pm_domain)
-		return qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg(qcom_iommu->sec_id, 0);
+	if (dev->pm_domain) {
+		ret = qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg(qcom_iommu->sec_id, 0);
+		if (ret) {
+			clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(CLK_NUM, qcom_iommu->clks);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
+	/* MSM8226 loses non-secure context state across MDSS power collapse. */
+	if (qcom_iommu->restore_ctx) {
+		for (i = 0; i <= qcom_iommu->max_asid; i++) {
+			struct qcom_iommu_ctx *ctx = qcom_iommu->ctxs[i];
+
+			if (ctx && ctx->domain && !ctx->secured_ctx)
+				qcom_iommu_program_ctx(qcom_iommu, ctx);
+		}
+		/* Finish context programming before the master resumes. */
+		wmb();
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
